WEBVTT

00:01.560 --> 00:06.150
Oh, boy. It's happening, huh?

00:06.150 --> 00:09.610
The day has come for Maki-kun 
to meet the full Umi family.

00:11.790 --> 00:13.450
I'm sorry for your loss.

00:13.850 --> 00:14.800
What?

00:14.800 --> 00:17.960
Amami-san would usually
 say something like...

00:18.340 --> 00:24.460
Lucky you! I wish I could have 
dinner at Umi's place, too!

00:24.980 --> 00:27.270
So what gives?

00:27.270 --> 00:30.740
Is Umi's dad that scary?

00:31.110 --> 00:35.220
My dad isn't scary or anything, okay?

00:35.580 --> 00:39.300
It's Riku you're afraid of, isn't it?

00:39.300 --> 00:40.440
"Riku"?

00:40.440 --> 00:45.440
Oh, your... older brother? 
I'm afraid I don't recall.

00:45.440 --> 00:48.520
Don't erase him from your memories!

00:45.970 --> 00:50.200
I can't believe she's reacting like this 
when she's friendly with everyone.

00:50.800 --> 00:53.560
What is Umi's brother even like?

00:54.300 --> 00:57.410
Good for you, though, Maki.

00:57.410 --> 01:02.090
You've got family dinner this week 
and the Christmas party the next.

01:02.090 --> 01:06.080
I didn't register for the party, 
so I won't get to go.

01:06.080 --> 01:08.010
Wait, what?

01:10.630 --> 01:15.350
Let's go talk to my sister and 
see what we can do, then.

01:15.350 --> 01:17.260
STUDENT COUNCIL OFFICE

01:16.050 --> 01:17.260
Nozomu.

01:17.800 --> 01:20.730
Why are you like this?

01:21.220 --> 01:23.380
Wait, Nozomu's sister...

01:24.270 --> 01:25.980
is the student council president?!

01:26.320 --> 01:29.250
Look, I get that I'm asking 
a lot out of nowhere.

01:29.250 --> 01:31.780
Just tell me if you can or can't.

01:32.190 --> 01:37.020
A bunch of people canceled, so we 
do have the leeway, numbers-wise.

01:37.020 --> 01:38.840
Hey, cool!

01:38.840 --> 01:41.160
Add Maki's name to the list, then...

01:41.160 --> 01:41.920
Ow!

01:41.920 --> 01:45.920
I'm not done, you dunce.

01:46.300 --> 01:49.250
Maehara-kun, was it?

01:49.250 --> 01:52.380
First off, thanks for being 
friends with my brother.

01:52.380 --> 01:53.720
Don't mention it.

01:53.720 --> 01:59.540
Anyway, I'm sorry for saying 
I want in at the last minute.

01:59.540 --> 02:01.060
You should be.

02:01.430 --> 02:06.730
The student council policy prohibits 
accepting requests after the deadline.

02:07.570 --> 02:11.280
But one of our members can't make it, 
and we do need a fill-in.

02:11.670 --> 02:15.190
As staff, you won't get to 
take part in any of the activities,

02:15.190 --> 02:18.900
but you're free to eat there 
during break time.

02:20.300 --> 02:22.660
Thank you, Prez!

02:22.660 --> 02:24.510
Let's go!

02:24.510 --> 02:25.160
Yeah.

02:26.720 --> 02:28.990
Good for you, Umi.

02:28.990 --> 02:30.380
How so?

02:34.310 --> 02:38.400
I'll get to spend Christmas with Umi!

04:09.510 --> 04:12.820
This should do, right?

04:14.010 --> 04:17.740
Thank you for inviting my son over.

04:18.460 --> 04:23.180
Oh, no, feel free to tell him what's what.

04:23.180 --> 04:24.380
Of course.

04:24.380 --> 04:27.040
I'll send him on his way, then.

04:28.570 --> 04:31.320
You didn't have to call them.

04:31.320 --> 04:33.430
I know, but I felt like it.

04:33.430 --> 04:36.630
I also wanted to talk to Sora-san again.

04:44.350 --> 04:47.890
Mom, did Dad say something to you?

04:49.030 --> 04:53.690
No. His messages are the same as always.

04:53.690 --> 04:54.700
Mom.

05:00.360 --> 05:05.990
Yeah, he found out the state 
I'd gotten into at work.

05:06.580 --> 05:10.830
He gave me a real earful. 
I know I deserved it, too.

05:12.020 --> 05:18.310
Mom hadn't told Dad about how busy work 
at her publishing company had gotten.

05:18.750 --> 05:19.900
When he found out,

05:19.900 --> 05:24.790
he scolded her for it, saying, 
"Why would you burden our son like that"?

05:25.640 --> 05:28.920
But does he really have the right?

05:29.370 --> 05:33.370
We can't really live our lives 
unless you work.

05:35.120 --> 05:36.300
Mom?

05:36.860 --> 05:38.860
Wait, am I wrong?

05:40.600 --> 05:46.730
Yeah. The truth is, I didn't have to 
work at all to put food on the table.

05:46.730 --> 05:50.120
Your dad sends us enough money 
every month to cover it all.

05:50.120 --> 05:52.650
Then why have you been paying for it?

05:53.260 --> 05:55.330
It was a matter of pride.

05:55.910 --> 06:02.220
I wanted to prove that I could handle things
without touching any of his money.

06:02.680 --> 06:08.220
Also, work kept my mind 
off of everything else.

06:08.790 --> 06:10.130
I'm sorry, Maki.

06:10.600 --> 06:13.230
We've selfishly put you through so much

06:13.500 --> 06:15.650
and made you feel so alone.

06:17.100 --> 06:19.360
But that all changes now.

06:19.820 --> 06:23.270
We can't be a family of three anymore,

06:23.740 --> 06:27.620
but I'll always be here for you, 
even if nobody else is.

06:28.820 --> 06:31.630
Anyway, we can talk about it later.

06:31.630 --> 06:33.160
You should get going.

06:34.230 --> 06:36.420
Welcome, Maki-kun!

06:36.850 --> 06:39.250
Thanks for coming all this way.

06:39.250 --> 06:41.460
No, thank you for inviting me.

06:41.740 --> 06:45.390
This is from my mom. It's nothing special, 
but she hopes you'll accept it.

06:45.390 --> 06:48.050
My, thank you very much.

06:48.050 --> 06:49.720
Now, come on in.

06:49.720 --> 06:52.180
Th-Thank you for having me.

06:59.490 --> 07:04.510
Are you gonna be okay, Maki? You look 
like you're about to have a heart attack.

07:08.470 --> 07:11.370
I-I'll be fine, probably.

07:19.170 --> 07:22.710
Dad, Maehara Maki-kun's here.

07:24.940 --> 07:28.840
Hello, Maehara-kun. 
I'm Daichi, Umi's father.

07:29.120 --> 07:32.060
I-I'm Maehara Maki.

07:32.340 --> 07:37.230
Let me thank you for taking the time 
to visit us during this busy time of year.

07:38.030 --> 07:41.440
Also, thank you for looking out 
for my daughter.

07:41.440 --> 07:43.790
Not at all... Umi...

07:43.790 --> 07:45.520
Wait, I mean...

07:45.520 --> 07:48.780
Feel free to address her 
the way you usually do.

07:49.210 --> 07:51.610
She's in high school now.

07:51.610 --> 07:55.660
It's not strange for her to have 
a few male classmates she's close to.

07:56.010 --> 07:57.370
Right...

07:57.370 --> 08:01.710
Come on, dear. You're scaring Maki-kun.

08:01.710 --> 08:07.660
Now, drop that tense expression 
and smile for us!

08:08.010 --> 08:12.210
Wh-What are you doing? 
In front of our guest, too!

08:12.210 --> 08:13.830
Help me out, Umi.

08:13.830 --> 08:14.840
Roger.

08:16.100 --> 08:17.600
S-Stop that!

08:18.350 --> 08:22.840
M-Maehara-kun, tell these two off for me!

08:23.570 --> 08:28.590
Wrong, dear. You mean "Maki-kun," 
not "Maehara-kun," right?

08:28.590 --> 08:31.410
Maki-kun! Please!

08:31.410 --> 08:35.400
Uh... Daichi-san can't take anymore.

08:31.840 --> 08:33.940
You're still too stiff!

08:35.400 --> 08:39.790
I'll loosen up as well, 
so could you please let him go?

08:36.460 --> 08:39.200
Stop it! Knock it off!

08:39.790 --> 08:43.620
Yeah? Okay, Umi, you can stop now.

08:43.620 --> 08:45.000
Got it.

08:46.140 --> 08:50.830
Maki-kun, um, I apologize 
for embarrassing myself like that.

08:50.830 --> 08:53.630
Well, you see what we're like.

08:54.270 --> 08:57.180
That's right. Isn't it fun?

08:57.560 --> 09:00.140
Y-Yeah.

09:00.140 --> 09:05.060
Mom, enough of the sketch comedy. 
Can we get dinner started?

09:05.060 --> 09:07.060
I'm starving.

09:07.060 --> 09:10.780
Right you are. 
Dear, could you get our son for me?

09:10.780 --> 09:11.840
Sure.

09:14.970 --> 09:17.290
What's your big brother like?

09:17.790 --> 09:19.660
He's an unemployed shut-in.

09:20.140 --> 09:23.170
Also, he's taken a massive liking to Yuu.

09:23.170 --> 09:27.230
He started crawling towards her 
this one time for no reason.

09:27.230 --> 09:29.010
It was creepy as all heck.

09:29.330 --> 09:30.630
Yeah...

09:30.630 --> 09:33.720
I can see why she wants to avoid him.

09:35.840 --> 09:38.180
Get down here, Riku.

09:40.660 --> 09:42.600
Why are you sitting there?

09:44.260 --> 09:46.900
We haven't had a guest over in ages.

09:46.900 --> 09:49.460
I have to show him the trademark 
Asanagi hospitality.

09:49.460 --> 09:51.620
I'll handle that!

09:51.620 --> 09:55.060
But then I wouldn't get 
to have fun with him!

09:55.060 --> 09:58.650
Umi, Mommy believes you 
shouldn't keep him all to yourself.

09:58.650 --> 10:00.750
I knew that was what you were after!

10:00.750 --> 10:02.250
Mom, Umi.

10:03.390 --> 10:07.210
Let's drop it there, 
or your dad will tell us off.

10:07.460 --> 10:12.840
Don't worry. I'll let you have 
the privilege of feeding Maki-kun.

10:13.900 --> 10:15.590
I-I'm not doing that!

10:15.590 --> 10:18.470
You're so stupid, Mom!

10:19.710 --> 10:24.090
Oh, right. Why don't we play some 
games after we're done eating?

10:24.090 --> 10:28.580
I got the latest entry in the series 
we always play at your house.

10:28.580 --> 10:31.940
Wait, you did? I so wanna play.

10:31.940 --> 10:35.430
Okay, so we're battling after dinner.

10:35.430 --> 10:38.910
So yeah, bro, we'll be using your room.

10:38.910 --> 10:43.370
Don't just waltz into my sanctuary.

10:43.370 --> 10:45.120
Also, that game's mine, not yours.

10:45.120 --> 10:48.730
Come on, you can afford 
to go outside for once.

10:48.730 --> 10:50.860
Where exactly do you want me to go?

10:50.860 --> 10:52.710
I dunno, the unemployment office?

10:53.510 --> 10:55.130
Like it'd be open at this hour!

10:55.130 --> 10:59.900
I know it's not. But you could easily 
look up job listings on your phone.

10:59.900 --> 11:01.310
Right, Dad?

11:01.310 --> 11:03.900
Yes. You heard her, Riku.

11:03.900 --> 11:04.840
Yes?

11:04.840 --> 11:07.400
Make sure you go first thing on Monday.

11:09.340 --> 11:10.810
Understood.

11:16.200 --> 11:18.210
Sorry about that, Maki.

11:18.210 --> 11:21.800
You're a guest, and you keep 
having to watch us squabble...

11:23.690 --> 11:26.250
Huh? What's the matter?

11:27.100 --> 11:30.420
Wait, Maki, you haven't realized?

11:38.320 --> 11:39.470
That smells good.

11:39.930 --> 11:42.460
What's for dinner, Mom?

11:42.460 --> 11:44.740
What could it be?

11:44.740 --> 11:46.440
Try guessing, Maki.

11:48.380 --> 11:49.600
Hamburg steak?

11:49.600 --> 11:51.760
Hey, bingo.

11:51.760 --> 11:55.940
You win a carrot glace 
for getting it right.

11:55.940 --> 11:58.320
What? I don't want carrot!

11:58.320 --> 12:02.200
Too bad. You need to stop being picky 
and eat your veggies,

12:02.200 --> 12:04.320
or you'll never grow up big and strong.

12:04.950 --> 12:06.390
I'm home.

12:06.390 --> 12:08.120
Dad! Welcome back!

12:09.470 --> 12:12.690
Hey, Maki. Were you a good boy today?

12:12.690 --> 12:13.420
Yeah.

12:13.420 --> 12:15.850
Don't let him fool you.

12:15.850 --> 12:19.750
He was just whining about 
not wanting to eat carrot.

12:19.750 --> 12:22.310
Is this true?

12:22.310 --> 12:24.970
That's not how a good boy behaves.

12:25.730 --> 12:27.020
Fine, I'll eat it.

12:28.070 --> 12:30.610
That's my son. Good boy.

12:33.470 --> 12:36.610
You really love Dad, don't you?

12:36.900 --> 12:39.650
Anyway, dinner's ready. 
Let's eat together.

12:39.650 --> 12:40.430
Yeah!

12:41.630 --> 12:45.620
Back then, I thought those times 
would last forever.

12:46.540 --> 12:49.950
But around the time 
I started middle school,

12:49.950 --> 12:53.570
we gradually stopped 
having dinners for three.

12:54.480 --> 12:56.340
Dad sure is late.

12:56.340 --> 13:00.780
Right? He even said he'd be home 
at a reasonable time tonight.

13:00.780 --> 13:03.570
I'm starting to get really hungry, 
so let's go ahead and eat.

13:03.570 --> 13:06.050
Otherwise, we won't get to
 eat until midnight.

13:06.590 --> 13:10.560
Yeah. I worked hard on tonight's dinner,
but it is what it is.

13:11.170 --> 13:14.880
The Maehara family dining table 
lost one member at first.

13:16.470 --> 13:19.520
For a while after that, 
it was just my mom and me...

13:20.580 --> 13:25.570
But she grew quieter over time 
as their marital issues intensified.

13:26.740 --> 13:29.260
We were both eating at the same table,

13:30.660 --> 13:35.930
but it felt like there was an invisible 
wall separating the two of us.

13:37.260 --> 13:40.050
And after my parents divorced,

13:40.810 --> 13:44.680
I was the only one left at the table.

13:46.030 --> 13:48.440
I... I'm so sorry.

13:48.440 --> 13:52.520
Why is this happening? I didn't mean to...

13:53.110 --> 13:54.240
Maki-kun?

13:54.240 --> 13:55.810
H-Hey...

13:56.140 --> 13:57.500
Are you okay?

13:57.500 --> 13:58.690
Sorry, Umi.

13:59.640 --> 14:03.570
I'm going to go get some 
fresh air and calm down!

14:03.570 --> 14:05.560
Wait, Maki!

14:06.280 --> 14:07.550
Maki...

14:16.760 --> 14:20.170
Ugh, what is wrong with me?

14:20.790 --> 14:24.040
Why did I have to go and cry 
in front of Umi's family?

14:24.790 --> 14:29.090
I feel so embarrassed, 
pathetic, and uncool.

14:29.710 --> 14:33.440
I'm a high schooler now. 
I'm not supposed to be such a baby!

14:33.910 --> 14:35.020
Maki!

14:36.180 --> 14:37.110
Umi?

14:40.790 --> 14:44.150
I'll be back in a bit, so stay inside.

14:44.150 --> 14:45.660
You moron!

14:45.660 --> 14:50.660
Do you really think I can just stay put 
after seeing my friend in that state?!

14:52.450 --> 14:55.330
I get it, but I want 
to be alone right now!

14:57.880 --> 15:01.500
Shut up! Stop trying to run!

15:01.500 --> 15:04.120
And let me take you into custody!

15:08.570 --> 15:10.140
Gotcha.

15:10.830 --> 15:13.020
You moron. Look at you.

15:13.380 --> 15:15.360
Your face is a mess.

15:16.020 --> 15:17.230
Sorry.

15:17.670 --> 15:19.940
It's okay. Come on.

15:19.940 --> 15:21.280
Come to me.

15:28.630 --> 15:33.430
I'm so ashamed. I acted like a child.

15:33.430 --> 15:36.540
We high schoolers 
are still kids, you know.

15:36.540 --> 15:41.750
We can get away with sniffling up to 
someone like this. Just barely, I think.

15:42.660 --> 15:45.110
Nobody else is here right now.

15:45.110 --> 15:49.150
Nobody's going to make fun of you.

15:50.030 --> 15:55.200
So stop worrying about it and 
entrust yourself to me, okay?

15:56.390 --> 15:57.640
I'm sorry.

15:58.250 --> 16:01.350
I think you mean "thank you."

16:01.350 --> 16:04.230
Right. Thank you, Umi.

16:08.070 --> 16:12.700
The thing with your parents 
was weighing on you after all?

16:13.020 --> 16:17.140
Yeah. I thought I'd gotten 
over it, but apparently not.

16:17.770 --> 16:21.500
Oh... You did well to hang in there.

16:28.430 --> 16:32.930
For now, forget about it all 
and give yourself up to me.

16:33.260 --> 16:35.840
You can think about it 
after you get some good sleep,

16:35.840 --> 16:41.400
eat a bellyful of food, 
and feel like yourself again.

16:41.660 --> 16:42.480
Okay.

16:42.940 --> 16:45.990
Just go to sleep like that for tonight.

16:48.590 --> 16:50.230
Good night, then.

16:50.750 --> 16:52.020
Thanks.

16:52.530 --> 16:54.490
Sure. Good night.

16:55.330 --> 16:59.860
Maki, remember that 
I'll always love you, okay?

17:05.250 --> 17:06.130
Heya.

17:07.020 --> 17:07.970
Heya.

17:10.630 --> 17:12.070
What time is it?

17:12.070 --> 17:15.350
Just past eight. Good thing it's Saturday.

17:15.770 --> 17:19.660
If you were awake, 
you could've gotten out of bed.

17:20.310 --> 17:23.690
I mean, I only woke up around an hour ago.

17:24.240 --> 17:27.780
Watching your sleeping face 
made the time fly by, so don't worry.

17:27.780 --> 17:30.570
I dunno. It sounds like I have more 
to worry about than I thought.

17:30.950 --> 17:33.160
So, how'd it feel?

17:33.580 --> 17:35.160
How'd what feel?

17:35.160 --> 17:38.620
Sleeping on my lap like a baby.

17:38.620 --> 17:40.620
Straight for the jugular, huh?

17:41.190 --> 17:42.710
Do I have to say it?

17:43.020 --> 17:46.130
It would make me happy if you did.

17:46.130 --> 17:50.220
In that case, it was c-comfy...

17:50.220 --> 17:51.080
And?

17:51.490 --> 17:53.080
Warm...

17:53.080 --> 17:53.720
Okay?

17:54.680 --> 17:57.930
And it smelled good?

17:57.930 --> 18:00.890
Perfect for a good night's sleep, then!

18:01.410 --> 18:03.850
That makes it all worth it.

18:04.130 --> 18:05.990
This is too one-sided.

18:05.990 --> 18:10.220
I haven't done anything to deserve 
you going out of your way for me.

18:10.220 --> 18:11.880
You're wrong about that.

18:12.790 --> 18:16.570
You've given me so much 
you have no idea about.

18:16.570 --> 18:18.940
In the time between us 
becoming friends and now,

18:18.940 --> 18:22.590
your kindness has given me 
so much strength, so many times.

18:23.330 --> 18:27.380
I only did what I did because 
that's what you did for me.

18:27.780 --> 18:28.880
That's all.

18:29.720 --> 18:30.700
Umi...

18:52.970 --> 18:54.650
Umi? Maki-kun?

18:55.730 --> 18:58.740
What exactly do you think you're doing 
first thing in the morning?

18:58.740 --> 19:00.120
S-Sora-san?!

19:00.120 --> 19:02.290
H-Hey, wh-what happened to knocking?

19:02.290 --> 19:05.420
I did knock. Several times.

19:05.680 --> 19:09.950
We need to have a talk 
once we're done with breakfast.

19:10.670 --> 19:12.130
Yes, ma'am.

19:13.200 --> 19:16.760
Listen, I'm not going 
to tell you not to kiss.

19:17.100 --> 19:20.230
Just please, think about 
the time and place.

19:20.230 --> 19:21.580
I'm sorry.

19:22.440 --> 19:26.580
If you don't, you'll cause 
a whole mess like we did.

19:26.580 --> 19:27.270
Honey?

19:28.070 --> 19:31.650
Why am I catching strays here?

19:31.650 --> 19:34.350
Are you? Maybe you're overthinking it?

19:34.350 --> 19:37.280
Anyway, that's all I had to say.

19:39.060 --> 19:41.740
Maki-kun, can we talk in private?

19:44.450 --> 19:49.170
My wife and daughter told me a little 
about your situation last night.

19:49.170 --> 19:54.180
Uh, I'm really sorry for breaking down.

19:54.180 --> 19:55.700
Don't worry about it.

19:55.700 --> 20:00.890
That kind of thing is a lot to take in, 
even for adults like ourselves.

20:01.190 --> 20:06.680
It must've taken a huge toll on 
a sensitive, gentle kid like you.

20:07.190 --> 20:09.730
You did great holding on 
by yourself, Maki-kun.

20:10.860 --> 20:11.900
Thank you.

20:11.900 --> 20:16.110
However, I do think you tried 
a bit too hard to carry the burden.

20:16.870 --> 20:22.330
It's not a bad thing to be considerate 
of your parents and their divorce.

20:22.590 --> 20:27.080
But that doesn't mean you have to 
completely bottle up your feelings.

20:27.650 --> 20:30.750
If you hold them in too long, 
your mind will give out someday.

20:31.530 --> 20:33.870
You should be able to understand that now.

20:33.870 --> 20:34.840
Right.

20:36.100 --> 20:39.950
Yeah, that dream I had over and over...

20:40.420 --> 20:42.800
was because I had something 
to say to both of them.

20:44.160 --> 20:48.210
Well, even if I begged and pleaded,

20:48.210 --> 20:52.730
it's not like my parents would make up 
just to indulge me, right?

20:53.500 --> 20:56.280
If it's too late to cry and complain,

20:57.130 --> 21:00.110
I'd rather hold it in 
than put them on the spot.

21:00.650 --> 21:04.670
Yeah. As you say, 
it won't change anything.

21:04.670 --> 21:07.700
Then it really is pointless.

21:07.700 --> 21:09.790
No, there is a point.

21:09.790 --> 21:10.460
Huh?

21:10.930 --> 21:13.810
If you cry, complain, and throw a tantrum,

21:13.810 --> 21:16.210
it will get that load off your chest 
if nothing else.

21:18.390 --> 21:23.010
It's okay to be honest with yourself 
and do what you want.

21:25.620 --> 21:26.760
I'm back.

21:26.760 --> 21:28.390
I'M OUT SHOPPING -MOM

21:30.660 --> 21:33.030
She was going through the album?

21:33.990 --> 21:36.820
This is such a good photo.

21:40.510 --> 21:42.170
I wish we could go back.

21:43.390 --> 21:47.910
It's okay to be honest with yourself 
and do what you want.

21:48.970 --> 21:51.320
I'm allowed to be more demanding.

21:51.790 --> 21:55.250
MEMORIES ALBUM
MAEHARA FAMILY

21:52.130 --> 21:54.140
Okay, I've decided.

21:55.720 --> 21:57.620
It's almost Christmas Eve.

21:58.100 --> 22:01.400
I'm going to take the day that marks 
one year since Dad and Mom divorced...

22:01.970 --> 22:05.970
CAN YOU DO ME A FAVOR?

22:02.360 --> 22:04.510
and make it a line in the sand.

